      "claim": "The economic relationship between medieval English lords and peasants was defined by the feudal system, which was inherently hierarchical and coercive.",
      "evidence": "Historical consensus on feudalism describes a system of mutual obligations where peasants (serfs) owed labor, rent, and various fees to lords in exchange for protection and land use, lacking modern concepts of free market negotiation.",
